Use a standard `<script>` tag in the component with `addEventListener` — Astro follows plain HTML and has no `onClick={...}` or `@click` syntax:

```astro
<button class="alert">Click me!</button>
<script>
  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('button.alert');
  buttons.forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      alert('Button was clicked!');
    });
  });
</script>
```

The script is bundled and runs only once per page even if the component appears multiple times, so query with `querySelectorAll` to attach the listener to every instance. For per-instance state, wrap the markup in a custom element and bind inside `connectedCallback()`.

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/client-side-scripts/

Import `StaticPaths` from `astro:static-paths` (added in `astro@6.0.0`) and construct it with an app instance, then call `getAll()` to retrieve every `{ pathname, route: RouteData }` that must be prerendered. This lets a custom prerenderer (set via `setPrerenderer()` in the `astro:build:start` hook) collect paths from within its own runtime, such as `workerd`. Note the module only provides a real implementation in the `prerender` Vite environment; elsewhere it returns a no-op implementation.

```js
import { createApp } from 'astro/app/entrypoint';
import { StaticPaths } from 'astro:static-paths';
const app = createApp();
const staticPaths = new StaticPaths(app);
```

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/adapter-reference/

Read `this.dataset.message` inside the custom element's `connectedCallback()`; the `data-message` attribute maps to the `message` key of `dataset`:

```html
<astro-greet data-message={message}>
  <button>Say hi!</button>
</astro-greet>
<script>
  class AstroGreet extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      const message = this.dataset.message;
      this.querySelector('button')?.addEventListener('click', () => alert(message));
    }
  }
  customElements.define('astro-greet', AstroGreet);
</script>
```

Frontmatter runs on the server, so `data-*` attributes are the mechanism for getting its values into the browser.

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/client-side-scripts/

Create the app with `createApp()` from `astro/app/entrypoint`, then pass it directly to `new StaticPaths(app)`:

```js
import { createApp } from 'astro/app/entrypoint';
import { StaticPaths } from 'astro:static-paths';

const app = createApp();
const staticPaths = new StaticPaths(app);

export const handler = (event, context) => {
  // do something with `staticPaths`
};
```

The app instance supplies the SSR manifest, route cache, and route component access the constructor needs.

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/modules/astro-app/

Construct `StaticPaths` from an app instance inside the handler and await `getAll()`, which resolves to `Array<{ pathname: string, route: RouteData }>`:

```js
import { StaticPaths } from 'astro:static-paths';
export function createHandler(app) {
  return async (request) => {
    const { pathname } = new URL(request.url);
    if (pathname === '/__astro_static_paths') {
      const staticPaths = new StaticPaths(app);
      const paths = await staticPaths.getAll();
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ paths }));
    }
    // ... handle other requests
  };
}
```

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/modules/astro-static-paths/

Two things ensure dynamic segments are handled: each dynamic route must `export` a `getStaticPaths()` returning its paths (otherwise `GetStaticPathsRequired` in static mode), and your prerenderer should collect those paths. Either wrap the default prerenderer via `setPrerenderer()` in the `astro:build:start` hook and delegate:

```js
'astro:build:start': ({ setPrerenderer }) => {
  setPrerenderer((defaultPrerenderer) => ({
    name: 'my-prerenderer',
    async getStaticPaths() {
      return defaultPrerenderer.getStaticPaths();
    },
    // setup(), render(), teardown()
  }));
},
```

or, in your target runtime, initialize `new StaticPaths(app)` and await `getAll()` to receive every `{ pathname, route }` needing prerendering.

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/adapter-reference/

Create `src/middleware.js` and export an `onRequest` function that logs the request URL and calls `next()` to continue rendering. 

```js
export function onRequest(context, next) {
  console.log(context.request.url);
  return next();
}
```

Call `await staticPaths.getAll()` on a `StaticPaths` instance (imported from `astro:static-paths`); it returns `Promise<Array<{ pathname: string, route: RouteData }>>` — a promise resolving to an array of objects each describing a prerendered path and its route data.

```js
import { StaticPaths } from 'astro:static-paths';

const staticPaths = new StaticPaths(app);
const paths = await staticPaths.getAll();
// Returns array of { pathname: string, route: RouteData }
return new Response(JSON.stringify({ paths }));
