Create a custom font provider by exporting a function that returns a `FontProvider` object with `name`, `init()`, `listFonts()`, and `resolveFont()` methods. Register it in `astro.config.ts` under the `fonts` array. The provider can accept config options (e.g., API token) and fetch fonts from a private registry in `init()`. Example:
```ts
// font-provider.ts
import type { FontProvider } from "astro";
export function registryFontProvider(config: { token: string }): FontProvider {
  let data: Fonts = {};
  return {
    name: "registry",
    config,
    init: async () => { data = await retrieveFonts(config.token); },
    listFonts: () => Object.keys(data),
    resolveFont: ({ familyName }) => data[familyName] ? { fonts: data[familyName] } : undefined,
  };
}
```
```ts
// astro.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from "astro/config";
import { registryFontProvider } from "./font-provider";
export default defineConfig({
  fonts: [{ provider: registryFontProvider({ token: "..." }), name: "Custom", cssVariable: "--font-custom" }]
});
```
Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/font-provider-reference/

Specify the version using the `version` family option in the font's `options` object. The default is `'latest'` and it only applies to CDN resolution.
```ts
{
  provider: fontProviders.npm(),
  options: { version: '5.0.0' }
}
```
Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/font-provider-reference/

The `config` property is a serializable object used for identification. It stores the provider configuration (e.g., API tokens, endpoints) passed when the provider is instantiated in `astro.config.ts`, making it available to `init()` and `resolveFont()`.
```ts
export function registryFontProvider(config: { token: string }): FontProvider {
  return { name: "registry", config, init: async () => { data = await retrieveFonts(config.token); }, ... };
}
```
Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/font-provider-reference/

Create `src/pages/posts/[slug].astro` and export a `getStaticPaths()` function that fetches all posts from Flotiq and returns an array of objects with `params: { slug: post.slug }` and `props: post`. Access the post data in the template via `Astro.props`.
```astro
---
import type { Blogpost } from "flotiq-api-ts";
import { flotiq } from "../../lib/flotiq";

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const posts = await flotiq.BlogpostAPI.list();
  return posts.data?.map((post) => ({ params: { slug: post.slug }, props: post })) || [];
}

const post: Blogpost = Astro.props;
---
<html lang="en">
  <title>{post.title}</title>
  <body>
    <h1>{post.title}</h1>
    <div set:html={post.content}/>
  </body>
</html>
```
Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/cms/flotiq/

In SSG, `getStaticPaths()` fetches ALL posts at build time and generates a route for each by returning `params: { slug }` for every post. In on-demand rendering, you access `Astro.params.slug` at request time to fetch a SINGLE post by filtering the API query with that slug.
```astro
// SSG: fetch all at build time
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const posts = await flotiq.BlogpostAPI.list();
  return posts.data?.map((post) => ({ params: { slug: post.slug }, props: post })) || [];
}

// On-demand: fetch one at request time
const { slug } = Astro.params;
const blogpostList = await flotiq.BlogpostAPI.list({ filters: JSON.stringify({ slug: { type: 'equals', filter: slug } }), limit: 1 });
```
Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/routing-reference/

Export a function that returns a `FontProvider` object with a unique `name`, an optional `init()` to fetch data (e.g. from your private registry), `listFonts()`, and `resolveFont()` returning `{ fonts }` for a matching family. Then register it in `astro.config.ts` under `fonts`:

