  prefetch: {
    defaultStrategy: 'load',
  },
});
```

```html
<a href="/pricing" data-astro-prefetch>Pricing</a>
```

The `load` strategy prefetches all opted-in links after the page has loaded, rather than on hover or viewport entry. (Note: with `<ClientRouter />`, `prefetchAll` defaults to `true`, so you'd set `prefetchAll: false` to limit prefetching to only these links.)

Since Astro v5, `params` returned by `getStaticPaths()` are no longer decoded automatically (they were decoded with `decodeURIComponent` in v4), so the percent-encoded string `'%5Bpage%5D'` is passed through verbatim into the URL and back into `Astro.params`. Fix it by decoding the value yourself with `decodeURI` when returning it:

```astro
---
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [
    { params: { slug: decodeURI('%5Bpage%5D') } }, // decodes to "[page]"
  ];
}
const { slug } = Astro.params;
---
```

Prefer `decodeURI` over `decodeURIComponent`, which decodes more than it should (e.g. `/`, `?`, `#`).

Return `{ params: { path: undefined } }` — setting a rest parameter to `undefined` generates the route with no remaining segments, i.e. the top-level `/docs` page in `src/pages/docs/[...path].astro`:

```astro
---
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [
    { params: { path: 'guide/intro' } }, // /docs/guide/intro
    { params: { path: undefined } },     // /docs
  ];
}
---
```

`undefined` is valid only for rest parameters; regular `[param]` values must be strings.

