In Astro 5.0, actions submitted via HTML forms are handled differently than RPC calls. When a form submits to an action, it's marked with `calledFrom: "form"` in the action context.

If your middleware only checks for `action?.calledFrom === "rpc"`, then form submissions will bypass that logic and not be evaluated by your session check.

To handle both RPC and form submissions, you should modify your middleware to also evaluate form actions. Here's how:

```ts
import { defineMiddleware } from 'astro:middleware';
import { getActionContext } from 'astro:actions';

export const onRequest = defineMiddleware(async (context, next) => {
  const { action } = getActionContext(context);

  if (action?.calledFrom === 'rpc' && action.name.startsWith('private')) {
    // Check for valid session token
  }

  // Handle form submissions too
  if (action?.calledFrom === 'form' && action.name.startsWith('private')) {
    // Add your session validation logic here
  }

  return next();
});
```

This ensures that both RPC and HTML form actions are checked for authentication.

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/modules/astro-actions/#getactioncontext

To protect pages and API routes with `@clerk/astro`, configure middleware and use `locals.auth()`.

