To properly type a prop in a component that receives a collection entry from the `blog` collection, use the `CollectionEntry` utility from `"astro:content"` with your collection name. This ensures full TypeScript support including autocompletion and type-checking based on your schema.

Example:
```tsx
// In a component receiving a blog post
import type { CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';

export default function BlogPost({ entry }: { entry: CollectionEntry<'blog'> }) {
  return <h1>{entry.data.title}</h1>;
}
```

This approach leverages the Zod schema defined for `blog` to provide accurate typing. The prop will have full autocompletion and type-checking based on your collection's frontmatter structure.

